# Frontend Conventions

## Structure
- Views in `frontend/src/views/` — one feature per `*View.vue`
- Shared UI in `components/`; logic in `composables/`
- API paths only via `ApiPaths` in `api/paths.js` — no scattered strings

## CRUD page pattern
```js
const { showForm, editing, form, openCreate, openEdit, closeForm } = useEntityForm(blankForm, { onReset: clearErrors })
```
- Wrap form in `<FormHost :show="showForm" @close="closeForm">`
- Desktop: hide list when form open (`v-show="!showForm || isMobile"`)
- Page title switches in desktop form mode via computed `pageTitle`

## API
- `api/client.js` attaches Bearer token; 401 → logout redirect
- **Global loader:** axios interceptors → `stores/loading.js` → `AppGlobalLoader`; opt out per request with `skipGlobalLoader: true`
- **List loading:** `AppSkeleton` (table shimmer) while page data loads; avoid plain «در حال بارگذاری…» text in list panels
- Use `trySubmit` from `useFormValidation` for field-level API errors
- **Form selects:** `useLookupsStore().getAccounts()` / `getCostTypes()` → `/api/lookups/*` by default
- **Admin CRUD lists:** pass `{ admin: true }` to hit full `/accounts` / `/cost-types` APIs
- Transaction attachments: `ApiPaths.incomeTransactionAttachment(id, attachmentId)` / `costTransactionAttachment(...)`

## Transaction attachments (income/cost)
- Permissions (no nav): `attachments.view` (list + preview), `attachments.add` (upload), `attachments.delete` (remove saved)
- **List:** `DocumentAttachmentList` only when `attachments.view`

## Audit metadata (all CRUD lists)
- Permission (no nav): `audit.view`
- **List/card:** no audit columns — clock icon in `RowActions` opens `AuditInfoPanel` (modal desktop / bottom sheet mobile with `useOverlayBack`); wire on accounts, persons, users, cost-types, general-types, food, income, cost
- API strips `audit` when caller lacks `audit.view` (same pattern as attachments)
- **Form:** `TransactionAttachmentsField` with `canView` / `canAdd` / `canDelete`
- **Preview:** `DocumentPreview` — image/PDF in modal (desktop) / bottom sheet (mobile)
- Edit mode: load `item.attachments` **after** `openEdit()` (not before — `onReset` clears them)
- Delete saved attachment in edit: immediate `DELETE` API; sync list row via `onExistingAttachmentsChange`
- Pending files: removed locally until form save
- Paths: `ApiPaths.incomeTransactionAttachment(id, attachmentId)` / `costTransactionAttachment(...)`
- **Server-side image processing:** client uploads raw files; API `FileStorageService` + `ImageProcessingService` on save — EXIF auto-orient first, then avatar face-crop or document warp **only when quad score ≥ threshold** (otherwise resize-only fallback for consistent output).
- **AvatarPicker** (profile / users / persons — **same component**): mobile sheet **`useOverlayBack`** (`appAvatarPicker`); **`capture="user"`**; **`scheduleInputClickAfterSheetClose`**. Inside **`FormHost`** (persons/users edit): `nativeFilePickerActive` defers overlay `history.back()` until the file is chosen — prevents form unmount/crash when returning from camera.
- **Mobile attach sheet:** close sheet via **`scheduleInputClickAfterSheetClose`**; `readInputFiles` is **async** (retries empty captures); toast via `emptyCaptureToast`; attachment sheets use `useOverlayBack` (`appAttachSheet`).
- **Avatar/person picture replace:** API deletes previous upload file from disk after successful save/remove (`FileStorageService.TryDelete`).

## Mobile overlay back (required for overlays)
Any mobile full-screen overlay, sheet, or preview **must** handle hardware/gesture back and top-bar back:
- Use `useOverlayBack(isOpen, requestClose, { enabled, stateKey })` from `composables/useOverlayBack.js`
- Always `history.pushState({ ...history.state, [stateKey]: true }, '')` — never wipe Vue Router keys or nav breaks (`…undefined/` SecurityError)
- `AppTopBar` calls `closeActiveOverlay()` before form back
- `FormHost` `onPopState`: skip if `hasActiveOverlay()`; only close form when `!history.state?.appForm`
- Register overlay in `activeOverlay` so top bar shows back on primary tabs when preview is open

## Auth & permissions
```js
auth.hasPermission('accounts.create')
auth.hasAnyPermission('users.update', 'users.delete')
```
Router: `meta: { permission: 'food.view' }`

## RTL & i18n
- `dir="rtl"` `lang="fa"`; use logical CSS (`inline-start`, `margin-inline`)
- Money: `formatMoney()`; digits in inputs: Persian allowed, store ASCII numbers
- Never pre-fill login credentials

## Lookups
- Use `useLookupsStore()` for accounts/cost-types/general-types dropdowns
- **AppSelect:** searchable by default (desktop + mobile); multi-token ALL-match + Persian normalize via `utils/selectSearch.js` (same idea as PersonSelect)
- **PersonSelect:** search via `ApiPaths.lookups.persons`; resolve selected id via `ApiPaths.person(id)`
- Person life status uses `isDead`: `PersonLifeStatus` badge **only when deceased** (same row as `NickBadge`); living people show no life badge
- Person **تاریخ وفات** (`deathDate`): edit/create form only when `isDead`; starts **empty** until user picks; not shown on Persons list or PersonSelect
- Person **لقب** (`nickName`): `NickBadge` on Persons list, PersonSelect, Income person column, person-income report
- Call `invalidate*` after mutating lookup data

## PWA
- Themes via `data-theme` on `<html>` (emerald, midnight, saffron, slate, plastic, plastic-dark)
- **Android standalone:** requires **HTTPS** (secure context) + registered service worker + manifest; HTTP home-screen shortcuts open inside Chrome with address bar — Settings shows `needsHttps` hint
- Production: serve `frontend/dist` over HTTPS; Docker default is HTTP `:8080` only (shortcut mode on phones)
- Mobile breakpoint: 768px (`useIsMobile`)
- Mobile datepicker mode (`stores/uiPrefs`): `sheet` (bottom wheels) | `modal` (calendar); Settings card only when `useIsMobile`; desktop always calendar modal
- `PersianDatePicker` mobile overlay (sheet or modal): `useOverlayBack` with `stateKey: 'appDatePicker'`
- **App updates:** `vite-plugin-pwa` `registerType: 'autoUpdate'` + `initPwaUpdate()` — new SW activates and reloads automatically; poll every 30m + on visibility restore
- **Exit on back (mobile):** `initPwaExitBack()` — on primary tabs, system back shows a bottom hint then leaves on second press within 2s; overlays/forms/nested routes still consume back first
- **List pagination:** `PagedListPanel` — desktop: page scroll + sticky thead/footer; mobile: inline bar after list (no fixed overlap with FAB)
- Install prompt: `usePwaInstall` / `PwaInstallBanner`
- `AppSelect` / `PersonSelect` mobile sheets: `useOverlayBack` (`appSelect` / `appPersonSelect`)
